Given the trajectory and the fact that the cannonball is still ascending at t=0.37 (as it is above robot 3), it will continue to rise, reach a peak, and then fall. It will hit robot 3 first as it descends, then robot 2, then robot 1. Since the cannonball is a projectile, it will hit the robots in sequence as it falls. The robots are small and will be destroyed by direct impact. The blocks are stationary and will not move until hit. The cannonball will hit robot 3 first, then robot 2, then robot 1. All robots will be destroyed by the cannonball's impact.

